0000:                   ********************************************************************
0000:                   * Dump - Show file contents in hex
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Dump follows the function of the original Microware version but now
0000:                   * supports large files over 64K, and is free from the problems of garbage
0000:                   * in wide listings.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * In addition it now allows dumping of memory modules and command modules
0000:                   * in the execution directory.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *   5      ????/??/??
0000:                   * From Tandy OS-9 Level One VR 02.00.00.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   6      2002/12/23  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Incorporated R. Telkman's additions from 1987, added -d option,
0000:                   * added defs to conditionally assemble without help or screen size check.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2003/01/17  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Removed -d option.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2003/01/21  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Narrow screen now shows properly, only dumps 16 bits worth of address
0000:                   * data to make room.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2003/03/03  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Fixed bug where header would be shown even if there was no data in a file.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   7      2003/06/06  Rodney V. Hamilton
0000:                   * Restored Rubout processing for terminals.
0000:                   
0000:                           nam     Dump
0000:                           ttl     Show file contents in hex
0000:                   
0000:                           ifp1
0000:                           use     defsfile
0000:                           endc
0000:                   
0000:                   * Tweakable options
0001:                   DOSCSIZ set     1       1 = include SS.ScSiz code, 0 = leave out
0000:                   DOHELP  set     0       1 = include help message, 0 = leave out
0050:                   BUFSZ   set     80
0000:                   
0011:                   tylg    set     Prgrm+Objct
0081:                   atrv    set     ReEnt+rev
0001:                   rev     set     1
0007:                   edition set     7
0000:                   
0000:                           org     0
0000:                   nonopts rmb     1
